sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant M as Bedrock model
  participant S as Strands agent
  participant H as Policy hook<br/>BeforeToolCallEvent
  participant P as Deterministic policy<br/>rooms + overlap
  participant DB as Postgres
  participant O as Email outbox<br/>SES
  participant HOST as Host
  participant W as Server action<br/>decideAction

  M->>S: tool use create_temporary_hold
  Note over HOST,DB: Hosts update existing pets/children policy with expected version.<br/>Only changed values increment version and audit.<br/>Settings and booking share the home advisory lock.<br/>Existing confirmed stays are not rewritten.
  S->>H: BeforeToolCallEvent (gated tool)
  H->>DB: loadDraftForTool: trusted draft,<br/>approvalStayHash, sanitized input
  H->>P: evaluateRoomSelection (capacity, overflow)
  H->>P: evaluateOverlap (beds, children, pets, special request)
  P-->>H: allow, interrupt, or deny
  H->>DB: audit policy_verdict {tool, decision, reason}

  alt deny
    H-->>S: event.cancel with reason text
    S-->>M: tool error, model explains to guest
  else allow, or approval already covers this stay
    H-->>S: continue, tool executes
  else interrupt
    H->>S: event.interrupt({name host_decision, reason})
    S->>DB: session snapshot saved in agent_sessions<br/>PostgresStorage, saveLatestOn message
    S-->>DB: run status interrupted, claim token cleared
    S->>DB: pending_decisions row<br/>(session, interrupt_id, reason)
    Note over DB: run-task.ts executeClaimedAgentTask
    O->>DB: selectPendingPings: one address per host
    O->>HOST: SES ping per eligible host<br/>on conflict (kind, source_id, host_id) do nothing
    HOST->>W: approve or decline, optional note
    W->>DB: pending_decisions status approved or declined,<br/>decided_by_host_id, note, application_error null
    W->>DB: enqueue task resume {sessionId, interruptId, response}
    W-->>HOST: redirect to run status page

    Note over S,DB: resume run claims the queued row
    S->>DB: verify decision matches host, status, and note
    S->>DB: applied_run_id set to this run
    S->>DB: restore session snapshot from agent_sessions
    S->>H: agent.invoke(InterruptResponseContent)
    alt declined
      H-->>S: event.cancel Declined by host, note
    else approved
      H->>P: re-evaluate current household policy,<br/>overlap and room selection
      H->>H: compare overflow fingerprint<br/>(rooms + arrangements)
      alt house changed to deny, or fingerprint differs
        H-->>S: event.cancel with reason
      else still allowed
        H-->>S: input.approvedBy = hostId, tool executes once<br/>booking transaction rechecks current state under home lock
      end
    end
    S->>DB: audit decision_applied {pendingDecisionId, runId}<br/>only if not already recorded
    S->>DB: run completed {summary, executedOn}

    opt resume run throws
      S->>DB: run failed, pending_decisions.application_error = message<br/>applied_run_id reset unless decision_applied exists
      DB-->>HOST: host panel shows the decision with a Retry button
      HOST->>W: Retry re-submits the same decision
      W->>DB: enqueue resume again
    end
  end
  Note over HOST,DB: Guest or host cancellation requires explicit review and POST.<br/>Withdrawal before booking retires queued work and decisions.<br/>Cancelled authority cannot resume into a new visit.<br/>Informational notes never become approval requests.
